    "text": "To determine how many coins Joanne has after the fourth hour, we need to follow the sequence of events and calculate the total number of coins collected and given away step by step.\n\n1. **First hour:**\n   Joanne collected 15 coins.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Coins after the first hour} = 15\n   \\]\n\n2. **Second hour:**\n   Joanne collected 35 coins.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Coins after the second hour} = 15 + 35 = 50\n   \\]\n\n3. **Third hour:**\n   Joanne collected 35 coins.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Coins after the third hour} = 50 + 35 = 85\n   \\]\n\n4. **Fourth hour:**\n   Joanne collected 50 coins.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Coins after the fourth hour} = 85 + 50 = 135\n   \\]\n   However, she gave 15 coins to her coworker.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Coins after giving 15 coins} = 135 - 15 = 120\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of coins Joanne has after the fourth hour is \\(\\boxed{120}\\).",
